n the United States and internationally. The company operates through four segments: U.S. Drilling, International Drilling, Drilling Solutions, and Rig Technologies. The company offers tubular running services, including casing and tubing running, and torque monitoring; managed pressure drilling services; and drilling-bit steering systems and rig instrumentation software. The company also offers drilling systems comprising ROCKit, a directional steering control system; SmartNAV, a collaborative guidance and advisory platform; SmartSLIDE, a directional steering control system; and RigCLOUD, a digital infrastructure that integrate applications to deliver real-time insight into operations across the rig fleet. In addition, it operates a fleet of land-based drilling rigs and marketed platforms rigs; manufactures and sells top drives, catwalks, wrenches, drawworks, and other drilling related equipment, such as robotic systems and downhole tools; and provides aftermarket sales and services for the installed base of its equipment. Nabors Industries Ltd. was founded in 1952 and is based in Hamilton, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony G. Petrello J.D. | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $24.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $229K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 106\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Nabors Industries Ltd. is a small-cap energy business with a $1.1B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $23M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 40% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (NBR) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_NBR_Volatility_111926071401_1795090441.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795090441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nabors Industries (NBR) Stock Looks Cheap As Shares Climbed 62%","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nabors-industries-nbr-stock-looks-021112684.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1794967872.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nabors Industries: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nabors-industries-3-key-takeaways-220503511.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795212303.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nabors Industries Lowers Receivables Facility Limit to $200M with Seventh Amendment","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/nabors-industries-lowers-receivables-facility-limit-to-200m-with-seventh-amendment","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795125356.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MrBeast Reaches Deal After Accusing Ex-Director of Stealing Secrets","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/mrbeast-reaches-deal-accusing-ex-192920000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795205037.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Geothermal Stocks Tied To Google\u2019s Clean Power Deal","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-nbr/nabors-industries/news/3-geothermal-stocks-tied-to-googles-clean-power-deal","date":"20